{
  "slug": "spec-to-code",
  "name": "Spec To Code",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Accelerates software delivery by automating SDLC stages inside Claude Code — Claude facilitates writing specs and designing architecture, then autonomously builds implementation plans, implements and tests the product — all driven by 13 structured /stc:* commands with built-in review gates and document consistency.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **11 skills** and **1 agent**.\n\n- **Skills** (11): `codebase-review` (Review the codebase for quality, consistency, and maintainability), `comment-code` (Add explanatory comments to code to improve readability and maintainability), `commit-code` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"commit\", \"commit changes\", \"create a commit\", \"stage and…), `create-plan` (Create a new implementation plan and task files in tasks/backlog/), `create-task` (Create a new task file in tasks/backlog/ — either a development task or a bug ticket), `define-product` (Definition stage — produce vision, product specification, and requirements in docs/), `design` (Architecture stage — produce high-level architecture document), `implement` (Execute implementation work — a single task or a plan (all phases or specific ones)), and 3 more\n- **Agents** (1): `stc` (spec-to-code SDLC agent)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install spec-to-code@claude-community` from `vkroz/spec-to-code`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 11,
    "agent": 1
  },
